  description: A crater is a bowl-shaped depression commonly formed when an asteroid,
    meteoroid, or other space object strikes a planetary surface. Craters are found
    on moons, planets, and other solid bodies, and their shapes can reveal information
    about past impacts.
  interestingFact: Earth has impact craters too, but erosion, weather, oceans, and
    geological activity gradually erase many of them.
  objectType: 8
